00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.500
So they're all over the world...

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.140
But how...

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.720
When I was surfing the web this
morning, it was business as usual...

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:42.220
I can't believe that it only took a few hours for the world to come to this.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.280
Don't you feel the same?

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:48.440
But there must be some place that's safe, right?

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.230
And soon, things will be back to normal.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.300
Keep dreaming.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:55.230
Do you really have to say it like that?

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:57.940
This is a pandemic. What am I supposed to say?

00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:59.550
A pandemic?

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:02.450
It's when an epidemic of infectious disease spreads.{From wiki, lol...}

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:06.230
So, the same disease that's infected people here is spreading throughout the world.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:08.120
Like influenza?

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.980
Like the Spanish Flu of 1918.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.260
Over 600 million people were infected by it, and 50 million people died from it.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.330
Think about recently when people were
worried about that new type of influenza.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.430
Isn't this more like the Black Death of the 14th century?

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.210
Europe's population went
down by a third during that.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.890
How did those diseases stop?

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.500
There are lots of theories, but...

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.520
The reason why diseases like those "die" is because they killed so many

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:40.760
that there's not enough people left to spread it.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:42.260
But...

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:47.860
In this case, the dead are moving around and attacking people.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:51.440
Then you are implying it has no reason to stop spreading?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.160
But it's so hot outside!

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:57.240
Maybe their flesh will start decomposing and they won't be able to move!

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:58.870
And what is the duration of this process?

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:03.170
Well, during summer, it takes around 22 days for some parts of the body to decompose.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.690
But during the winter, it can take months...

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:08.770
Anyway, if we go to our homes—

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:11.010
How do we know they'll even start to decompose?

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.260
Why do you say that?

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:17.960
Don't these things defy our knowledge of medicine? So why bother relying on it?

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.310
It could be hopeless. Just how long...

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:26.910
What is important is having a location to
make use of after we check on our families.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:31.040
Should we act only in our own
self-interest, we stand not a chance.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:33.750
Let us act as a team.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.100
We should help survivors as our ability allows us to.

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:44.160
Got it.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:45.960
How do we get out?

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:49.550
The front door is closest to the parking lot.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:52.340
Let's go!

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.330
Just to confirm,

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.090
you need not begin fighting unless it is inevitable.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.000
Refrain from fighting when the opportunity arises.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.140
They only respond to sound.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.930
Additionally, they're powerful enough to break down a normal door.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:20.330
So once they get a hold of you, you're gonna get eaten.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:21.450
Be careful.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:25.970
Takuzo!

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:26.860
Shit...

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.080
Stay back!

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.520
Th-Thank—{"T-Thank" to "Th-Thank" -A0}

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.580
Not too loud.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:55.970
Is there a person among you with a bite?

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:57.890
Nope!

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.090
They really do look fine.{inc. hontoni}

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.810
Wanna come with us? We're gonna get outta here.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:06.780
Y-Yes!

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:14.700
A bunch of them are down there.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:20.360
What's the point of hiding here?
They use their ears, not their eyes.

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:22.680
Then why don't you prove that for us, Takagi?

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:29.280
Regardless, if we remain inside of the school as such, we will be unable to move once attacked.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.600
No way out but through the gate, huh.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:36.680
We require someone to validate
the truth behind Takagi-kun's words. {"validify" to "validate" for flow -A0}

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:42.200
I'll go.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.060
No Takashi, I'll—

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:46.890
It would be more preferable if I were to go ahead of you.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:51.100
You should stay back in case
something happens, Busujima-sempai.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.140
But why, Takashi?!

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.270
Who knows?

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.820
"Who knows"?

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:03.230
Really, who knows?

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:05.700
Takashi—

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.030
I understand how you feel.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.470
Regardless, this decision was made by no one but himself.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:47.600
<i>They really can't see me?</i>

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:50.660
<i>In that case...</i>

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:33.890
RUN!

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:38.710
Why'd you do that?!

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:43.450
If you hadn't yelled, we'd probably only
have to worry about the ones close to us!

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:48.290
No way! Didn't you hear that echo?

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.550
There's more of them!

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.150
Don't talk.

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:04.280
Run!

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:06.890
RUN!

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:44.550
Takuzo!

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:45.580
Naomi!

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:46.570
Run!

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.340
Takuzo!

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:49.220
Forget him!

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:50.900
There's no point in trying to save him if he's already been bitten!

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:55.230
Wait—

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:56.840
Why?

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.390
I told her it's useless.

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:00.260
Why is she going back for him?

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.060
I... understand.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:06.000
With the whole world gone to hell,

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.270
I'd much rather die with the one I love.

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:12.450
What kind of doctor are—

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:13.060
Watch out!

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:17.150
Please calm down, Takagi-san!

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:18.730
You filthy nerd!

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:21.930
Who gave you the right to
interrupt me while I'm talking?

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:23.880
Well...

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:25.610
I don't know.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:30.300
I envy your close relationship.

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:33.480
Sensei, the key!

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.020
Target? Check.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:41.650
Public safety? Check.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.370
Ready to rock and roll!

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.350
Oh hurry up and shoot them already!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.970
Komuro-kun, they're all in!

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:53.250
You first, Sempai!

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.860
This isn't like my car!

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:01.470
Uhm... The gas, the brake, the clutch...

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:03.100
Help us!

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:11.510
Who's that?

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:13.530
That is Shidou. He teaches 3-A.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:15.600
Shidou...

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:17.470
We're ready to go!

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:18.810
Hold on a bit!

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.250
There're some swarming in the front too.{"There're" -A0}

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:23.610
I can't drive if there're too many of them bunched together!{"There're" -A0}

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.210
So run them over!

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:28.230
If we do that with this bus, we'll end up rolling over!

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.380
Don't save him!

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.760
Rei, what's your problem?

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:35.960
You don't need to save him!

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:38.060
We should leave him to die!

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.140
Everyone! Hurry!

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:42.190
I guarantee you'll make it out alive.

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:44.300
Okay, Sensei!

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:48.340
<i>Despite what I said, I wonder if they'll even make it to the bus.</i>

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:55.450
I sprained my ankle!

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:57.430
Oh...

00:12:58.550 --> 00:12:59.720
Is that so?

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:03.150
Then it's the end for you.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:11.220
The world as we knew it has come to an end.

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:13.410
In this world,

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.580
it's the survival of the fittest.

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:28.490
Shizuka-sensei!

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:29.300
We're off!

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:35.240
To the gate!

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:36.190
I know!

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:47.360
They're not humans.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.990
They're not humans anymore!

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:14.940
Looks like we made it.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:15.890
Yeah.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.190
Thank you for saving us.

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:20.470
Are you the leader, Busujima-san?

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.020
We are without one.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:24.470
Our survival is simply the product of our team work.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.850
Well that's no good.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:30.990
A leader is required in order for us to survive.

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:33.940
One who manages everything.

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:35.820
You're going to regret this.

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:39.230
You're definitely going to regret saving him.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:41.910
Our city!

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:34.210
Look!

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:37.100
We'll never make it if we keep going!

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:41.760
First off, why do we have to do
whatever you guys planned to do?

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:45.450
You all decided to go back to the city without asking us.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:49.340
Couldn't we have just looked for a safe place inside the school?

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:50.950
He's right!

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:54.480
We should find a place to hide, like that convenience store we just passed by.

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:01.190
I've had it!

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:03.260
I can't drive with all of you yelling!

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:07.380
What... the hell?!

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:10.320
Then what do you wish to do?

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.170
I can't...

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.520
I can't stand this guy!

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:19.300
Why?

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.270
What did I ever say to you?

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.530
You...

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:34.890
You suck.

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:40.480
Splendid work.

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:45.890
Komuro-kun, Miyamoto-san,
 that was some excellent teamwork.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:52.960
But, hmm... The fact that this conflict
arose simply proves what I stated earlier.

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:56.610
We really do need a leader.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:58.110
Do you understand?

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:01.620
And there's only one person who can do the job?

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:07.090
Well Takagi-san, I'm a teacher and the rest of you are students.

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:11.180
That alone should be enough to say who's more qualified.

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:16.690
If I was the leader, I would prevent conflict.

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:19.150
What do you all say?

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.130
Well that's that.

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:37.950
I've become the leader based on a majority vote.

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:45.890
Rei!

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:48.420
Screw it!

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:52.050
No way in hell am I going to be anywhere near him!

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:54.210
Rei...

00:17:56.490 --> 00:18:00.380
If you're saying that you can't get along,
 then we'll just have to split.

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:02.310
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:06.160
Komuro!

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:07.440
Wait!

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:10.500
You just have to put up with him until we get to the city.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.000
Besides, it's way too dangerous to—

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:14.240
Didn't I tell you that you'd regret this?!

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:16.320
Look, now's not...

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:22.100
Dr. Marikawa!

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:51.060
Now we're split...

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.500
Komuro-kun! Are the two of you unharmed?

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.080
The police station!

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:08.400
We'll meet at the East Police Station.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:10.260
At what time?

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.410
7 PM!

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:16.080
If it doesn't work out today,
then we'll try again tomorrow!

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.570
Dr. Marikawa, we are unable to advance.

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:34.640
Okay, I'll turn back and find another route.

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:42.720
Crap. Let's get out of here!

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:16.030
You...

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:18.720
You piece of crap...

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:39.300
Takashi.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:45.010
Let's go.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:02.120
Kuroku Somaru Sora no Shita

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:02.120
Under the sky that has lost its light,

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:02.120
黒く染まる空の下

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:06.380
Kage ni Obie Nokosareta

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:06.380
I was left behind, trembling in the big shadow

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:06.380
影に怯え残された

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:11.080
Akaku Moeru Chi no Iro ga

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:11.080
The blood, burning in scarlet red,

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:11.080
赤く燃える血の色が

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:15.520
Nijinda Mama Tokete Yuku

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:15.520
melts away in its blotted color

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:15.520
滲んだまま溶けてゆく

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:18.400
Mou Ichido Mayowazu

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:18.400
It's not remotely possible

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:18.400
もう一度迷わず

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:24.290
Ano Koro no Bokura ni Modoreru Hazu mo Nai

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:24.290
for us to go back to who we used to be

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:24.290
あの頃の僕らに 戻れるはずもない

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:26.930
Return to destiny

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:26.930
Return to destiny

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:32.900
Ai Suru Kotoba Mitsukete Inori wo Komete

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:32.900
I found those sweet words and added them to my prayers

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:32.900
愛することは見つけて　祈りを込めて

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:38.680
Dareka no Tame ni Tatakau Sube wo Shitta

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:38.680
I learned how to fight for my loved ones

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:38.680
誰かのために戦う術を知った

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:43.680
Soredemo Kimi wo Nakusu to Shitara

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:43.680
If I'm unable to remain with you,

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:43.680
それでも君をなくそうとしたら

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:47.080
Boku wa Kono Inochi wo

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:47.080
I'll give up my life

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:47.080
僕はこの命を

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:53.750
Sasagete Demo Kimi no Soba ni Iru yo

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:53.750
so I can be by your side

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:53.750
捧げてでも　君のそばにいるよ

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:28.050
Are we going to walk to the city?

00:22:28.930 --> 00:22:30.780
If we don't have another way, yeah.

00:22:31.940 --> 00:22:35.100
Wait, he was wearing a helmet...

00:22:49.470 --> 00:22:50.980
I didn't know you had a license.

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:55.450
High schoolers have the right to drive without a license!

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:10.840
<i>In other words, I didn't know yet</i>

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:16.330
<i>that this world had already ended.</i>

00:23:26.700 --> 00:23:29.350
{Takashi}Well excuse me for not being Hisashi!

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:34.200
{??}I saw my family turn into those things with my very own eyes!

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:33.160
{Rei}Takashi!
